<title>USA: Favorable weather continues for Brazil coffee - WSC.</title>
<headline>Favorable weather continues for Brazil coffee - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The coming week should see continued warm, high pressure dominating Brazil's coffee belt, Weather Services Corp said in an update on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Fair to partly cloudy skies were observed in the coffee belt this morning. Low temperatures have remained in the upper 50's to low 60's F (middle teens C).</p>
<p>Fair to partly cloudy skies are expected for the next seven days. Temperature levels should stay near to above normal. Low temperatures should range in the 50's to low 60's F (low to middle teens C).</p>
<p>The high pressure system will prevent any cool air from entering the region, according to WSC. &quot;Harvest weather will be quite favorable,&quot; WSC said.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
